<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN SUGAR BEET PLANTINGS JUMP IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN SUGAR BEET PLANTINGS JUMP IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian sugar beet plantings stood at 71.69 percent of the planned total on April 7, the Belgian sugar beet institute (IRBAB) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The institute gave no figure for the total area planted so far because data from two factories were not yet available.</p>
<p>At the last planting survey on March 31 the total stood at 8,445 hectares, or 8.23 percent.</p>
<p>The planned area for 1997 is 102,262 hectares, down from 103,849 hectares in 1996.</p>
